Arara Code: generic extension-owned blocking and overlay webview modals.

Why a patch: the public/proposed webview API has no blocking modal, CannotClose
capability, lifecycle veto, command admission hook, or transparent-frame overlay
modal. Reuse the native modal editor and its existing focus/layout machinery
instead of intercepting DOM keys or reopening a closed tab. The extension
supplies arara.modal.viewType and an exact arara.modal.allowedCommands list for
a blocking modal (clearing the viewType releases the gate; CannotClose prevents
editor/modal dismissal; closing the window stays possible). For a dismissible
overlay modal that keeps the workbench visible behind it, the extension supplies
arara.overlayModal.viewType without blocking commands or hiding the workbench.
No setup steps, provider names, business decisions or process execution here.
Touches: command service, webview editor input/service, native modal part/CSS.

